---
title: Alaskan Halibut
servings: 2
rating: 4
description: Alaskan Halibut can dry out very quickly if overcooked. It is a very versatile fish to cook with, as the dense, meaty flesh holds up well to many different cooking methods. Serve with roasted asparagus or lemon basil angel hair pasta.
source.name: Festival Foods
tags: Fish
---

= All Preparations =
@halibut filets{12%oz}, @oil{2%Tbsp} or @butter{2%Tbsp}, @Penzey's Muskego Ave. Seasoning{2%tsp}

= Bake =
Bake fish in a baking dish that has been greased or lined with foil. 
Brush fish with generous amounts of oil or melted butter and seasonings. 
Bake at 400F for approximately ~{10%minutes}.
Baste with additional oil or butter halfway through.

= Pan Sear =
Pan sear fish in a pan with oil over medium-high heat for 5-7 minutes per side.
Add 2 Tbsp oil after flipping fish.
When ready, the skin will be crisp and flesh will be firm.

= Grill/Broil =
Grill or broil using medium-high heat.
Brush fish with oil, and grill or broil skin side up for ~{6-8%minutes} per side, or ~{10%minutes} per 1-inch of thickness.
